## Summary

Review of the `agents-arwaky` unified tool orchestrator: a polyglot multi-agent ecosystem (Rust/Node/Python) with a central `aa`/`arwaky` CLI, XDG-compliant per-tool installers/uninstallers, MCP config generation, harness connector/disconnector, skill manager, backup/restore (incl. Google Drive), and daemon managers (Anytype, 9Router). Scope covers `tools/cli`, `tools/lib`, `tools/install`, `tools/uninstall`, `tools/skill`, `tools/connect`, `tools/backup`, `tools/daemons`, `tools/mcp`, and representative `tools/skills/*` scripts. Overall the codebase is well-structured with good security hygiene (path-containment helpers, `filter="data"` tar extraction, 0600 secret files, fail-closed config merges, env-file secret passing). Findings below are correctness/DRY/error-propagation issues, not exploitable vulnerabilities.

## Findings

### Security
| # | Severity | Issue | Location | Recommendation |
| --- | ---------- | ------- | ---------- | ---------------- |
| S1 | 🟡 WARNING | Path-containment guard is a **no-op** in the `--dest …/*.md` branch: `ensure_under(dest.parent, dest)` always passes because `dest` is trivially inside its own parent. This gives a false sense of traversal protection (bypass pattern). | `tools/skill/skill.py::copy_single_skill` / `remove_single_skill` | Drop the misleading `ensure_under` for the explicit-file case (user-supplied `--dest` is intentionally arbitrary) **or** validate against an allowed root. Keep `ensure_under` only where a real base dir exists. |
| S2 | 🟢 INFO | A personal email is hardcoded as the credentials fallback default (PII in source). | `tools/backup/gdrive.py::get_credentials` | Remove the hardcoded `arwaky90@gmail.com` default; discover the credential file or fail with a clear message. |

